Z||000000||Loki||02-25-2001||01:04 PM||||When my Fiero is rolling im getting a load popping form the front drivers side... Im thinking its the ball joints but could I be wrong?<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||terryk||02-25-2001||01:28 PM||||Could be. Ball joint usually clunk when the tire goes up and down or on very hard turns.<P>Take it for a drive over some railroad tracks. They will be obvious if they are loose/worn. <P>Then remove the wheel and pry between the lower control arm and knuckle. Any play is bad. Repeat for the top.<P>There is a spring in the joint which is why it's important to check them under load if possible. They can appear tight while pushing them around with your hands and still be bad.||||reg||1
